==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|un|roll|lang=en}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[straighten]] something that has been [[roll]]ed, [[twist]]ed or [[curl]]ed.
#: ''Unroll your sleeping bag and spread it on the floor of the tent.''
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To [[emerge]], be [[reveal]]ed or become [[apparent]]; to [[unfold]].
#: ''We will have to see how the events '''unroll'''.''
# {{context|transitive|programming|lang=en}} To replace (a [[loop]] in a [[program]]) with a [[repetitive]] [[sequence]] of the individual [[instruction]]s that the loop would carry out, sometimes used as an [[optimization]].

====Related terms====
* [[unfold]]
* [[unfurl]]

